# History store (043 A2/A3): snapshot files are content-addressed and
# never rewritten — cache for a year, immutable. The index is append-only
# — revalidate often so new snapshots surface.
#
# Workers static assets apply ALL matching rules and comma-join a header
# that appears in two of them, so the index detaches the wildcard rule's
# Cache-Control with `!` in the SAME block before setting its own — the
# verified shape (wrangler dev 4.146.0, 2026-10-02): a lone detach block
# before a second set block gets lost, and a plain second value joins as
# "…, max-age=60" with the year max-age first and winning the RFC-9111
# first-max-age rule.
/data/history/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/data/history/index.json
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=60
